  "question": {
    "text": "A series LCR circuit with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>mH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>, is connected across an AC source of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> supply. The power factor of the circuit would be ____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The capacitive reactance of the circuit is given by, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The inductive reactance of the circuit is given by, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>ω</mi><mi>L</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>From above calculations, it is clear that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math> Power factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
